WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:02.510
- All right y'all, I can't let you go

00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:04.470
without one more story
of hope and goodness.

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.807
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.807 --> 00:00:08.620
(high-energy rock music)

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.780
She is one of the most talented
and inspiring entertainers

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.560
in American history, a
living national treasure.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.890
I love her so much. In
fact, our love for her

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:19.810
is possibly the only thing we
all can agree on these days

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.230
in this divided world.

00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.860
I don't know one person
doesn't love this woman.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:25.421
I'm talking about the one
and only, Miss Dolly Parton.

00:00:25.421 --> 00:00:26.700
(crowd cheers)

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.058
And now I'm excited to
say her story is coming

00:00:30.058 --> 00:00:31.927
to a new generation.

00:00:31.927 --> 00:00:35.070
"I am Dolly Parton" by
Brad Meltzer is out today

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.237
and it's the latest in his

00:00:36.237 --> 00:00:38.548
"Ordinary people change
the world" book series

00:00:38.548 --> 00:00:41.668
featuring famous leaders,
like Oprah Winfrey,

00:00:41.668 --> 00:00:44.470
Abraham Lincoln, and Rosa Parks.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:46.990
Um, here to talk about it
is author Brad Meltzer.

00:00:46.990 --> 00:00:48.379
Give it up for him y'all.

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:50.760
(crowd cheers)

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.775
Nice to see you again, Brad.

00:00:53.775 --> 00:00:54.810
- Hey, everybody.

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:55.643
- Oh, hey.

00:00:55.643 --> 00:00:56.660
(crowd cheers)

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.920
So, it's, it's so great to see you.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:01.140
I love that you did this book,

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:02.300
but what do you think, kids,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.890
what do you think they're
gonna love about Dolly's story?

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:07.090
- Listen, you know, we wrote
these books to give our,

00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:09.270
my own kids better heroes, to look up to.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.540
What I think they're gonna love is

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:13.580
you get to see her as a
person and how human she was.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:16.240
When Dolly Parton was
growing up, she was so poor

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.890
that on the day she was born,

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.640
that her father paid the
doctor with a sack of cornmeal.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.810
Her mother fed her love of books.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.190
And Dolly's, one of her
favorites, as a little girl

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.660
was "The Little Engine That Could,"

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.990
and that's who Dolly Parton
is. She's the little engine.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.180
Instead of wearing what
everyone tells her to wear,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:35.190
she says, maybe I can
wear flashy costumes.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.800
And she does. Instead of
just singing country songs,

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:39.590
she sings songs that
everyone's gonna love.

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:42.080
Instead of being just a music
star, she's a movie star.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:44.120
And then she says, I'm gonna
open up my own theme park.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.540
And they say, that'll never work.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.260
She doesn't listen to any
of the business people

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:48.860
who tell her that. She opens up Dollywood

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:51.939
and then starts her own charity,
the Imagination Library.

00:01:51.939 --> 00:01:52.772
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah.

00:01:52.772 --> 00:01:54.430
- Which gives away
millions of books to kids

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.690
around the country.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:57.887
You know what the very first
book they started with?

00:01:57.887 --> 00:01:59.300
- [Both] "The Little Engine That Could."

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.570
- Oh, I love that. She's also just

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.430
like the epitome of what one
should be in the spotlight.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:11.430
Like she's so like, graceful
and caring and, and empathetic.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.190
Like, she's just a really,
really cool person as well.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:16.620
Um, and sometimes, you
know, when you see people,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.630
you know at the top like
that, they're not always,

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:20.090
they're not always, um, nice.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.260
And, and she's so lovely and she's so kind

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.170
and that's something to
love about her as well.

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:25.970
But, what do you think surprised you most

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.360
about Dolly's story?

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:28.730
- You know, it's this Kelly, and it's,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:31.920
it's actually the one thing
that she has in common with you

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:33.600
and you have it with her.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.310
At her concerts, just like at your show,

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:38.200
you can find old and you can find young,

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.970
you can find rich and poor

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:42.540
and gay and straight, city
folks and country folks,

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.250
and Black and white and
everything in between.

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.420
She loves them all.
And she, just like you,

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.440
doesn't judge you as long
as you're being yourself.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.840
And I wanna read to you,
this is the final page

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:56.120
from "I am Dolly Parton" by
myself, my favorite author,

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:56.953
Brad Meltzer.

00:02:56.953 --> 00:02:58.690
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:00.860
Um, and this is what it says.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:03.400
It says, "There's only one
thing you gotta be in life,

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.090
yourself. Whatever you
are be authentically that.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:09.273
And the people who look, sound
or think different from you,

00:03:09.273 --> 00:03:11.230
love them for who they are.

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.494
Your dreams are worth dreaming.

00:03:12.494 --> 00:03:14.180
Your songs are worth singing.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:17.530
Your story is worth
telling, just as it is.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:20.610
Be proud of who you are and
don't ever limit yourself.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.940
I am Dolly Parton and I see the light

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.411
that shines within you."

00:03:24.411 --> 00:03:25.608
(crowd applauds)

00:03:25.608 --> 00:03:28.920
- Aww. It's so perfect for her too.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.950
Like she's so that person.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:32.439
Thank you so much, Brad.

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:33.460
(crowd applauds)

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.980
- Thank you so much again.

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.260
- All right, I'm liking
your post right now.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.330
And everybody be sure to
pick up "I am Dolly Parton"

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.118
as well as another one of
Brad's books, "I am I.M. Pei"

00:03:44.118 --> 00:03:47.570
about famed Chinese American
architect, I.M. Pei.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.880
Um, that's not all though.

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.120
Our season long partner
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.982
the go-to pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:56.060
want to honor ultimate
overachievers just like you.

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:58.500
So, they're gonna be writing
a check for a thousand dollars

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.130
to Dolly Parton's Imagination
Library in your honor.

00:04:02.130 --> 00:04:05.132
The Imagination Library helps
inspire a love for reading

00:04:05.132 --> 00:04:08.670
early in life by gifting books,
to children five and under

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.446
for free, which is amazing.

00:04:10.446 --> 00:04:12.653
Uh, thank you so much, Brad.

